# try does NOT catch DepthExceeded (E040) — system-level limits propagate.
# This verifies the non-catchable semantics: try wrapping collect on an infinite range
# still surfaces the depth error rather than wrapping it in Variant(Error, ...).
# DepthExceeded fires at ~256 elements before ResourceLimitExceeded (E043, 1M elements).
# Both have the same non-catchable semantics in builtin_try (builtins_meta.rs:222-227).
[try [fn [] [collect [range 0]]]]
=== error
[E043] collect: exceeded maximum collection size (1000000). Use $take to limit infinite sequences before collecting. (defined at stdlib/prelude.llt:2460:15-2460:35)
  --> stdlib/prelude.llt:2460:15-2460:35
   |
  2460 | """] [let xs] [builtin-collect xs]]
       |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  in [builtin-collect ...] at stdlib/prelude.llt:2460:15-2460:35
   |
  2460 | """] [let xs] [builtin-collect xs]]
       |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  in materialized at 5:1-5:34
  in [try ...] at 5:1-5:34
